{"texts": ["DEPARTMENT OF HOUSING AND URBAN DEVELOPMENT  Series and Series Number: \n(Supersedes issue dated  \n    March 4, 1998) \nHousing - Federal Housing Commissioner  MATERIALS RELEASE NO:   1216c\n  \n \n   \n  \n TO:  DIRECTORS, SINGLE FAMILY HOCs    \n DIRE CTORS, MULTIFAMILY HUBs  ISSUE DATE \n  \n July 8, 2003 \n \n      REVIEW DATE                \nJuly 8, 2006  \n \n \nRUBEROID \u2013 Modified Bitumen Roofing SUBJECT:  1.  Product \n \n \n2. Name and address  \n of Manufacturer \n  \n  \n  \nGAF Building Materials Corporation \n1361 Alps Road \nWayne, NJ  07470-3689 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nData on the nonstandard product described herein have been reviewed by the Department of Housing and \nUrban Development (HUD) and determination has been made that it is considered suitable from a technical \nstandpoint for the use indicated herein. This Release does not purport to establish a comparative quality or \nvalue rating for this product as compared to standard products normally used in the same manner. \n \nThis Materials Release cannot be used as an  indication of endorsement or approval by HUD of the described \nproduct, and any statement or representation, however made, indicating such approval or endorsement by \nHUD is unauthorized. See Code 18, U.S.C. 709. \n \nAny reproduction of this Release must be in its entirety. \n \n \n \n \n \n \nUSE: RUBEROID roof systems are installed as single and multi-ply roofing construction that \ncan be used on nominally flat to 3 in/ft roof slopes.  The roofing system can be used in all \nareas of the contiguous U.S., and can be laid over any type deck and/or insulation which \nis acceptable to the GAF Materials Corporation. \n \n NOTE:  Nominally flat means the roof shall have a minimum slope of 1/4 inch per foot. \n \nDESCRIPTION: \n \n The GAF RUBEROID Modified Bitumen (MB) roofing membrane has a polyester mat \ncore with modified bitumen applied on each side of the core.  RUBERIOD MB is \nmanufactured in three different membranes: \n \n  1.  Smooth Surfaced Torch Applied \n  2.  Granule Surfaced Torch Applied \n  3.  Granule Surfaced Mop Applied \n \n RUBEROID MB can be used in the construction of flashing in addition to membrane. \n-2- \n \nMATERIALS: \n \n All materials for these roof systems shall be supplied by GAF Materials Corporation, or \nits approved roofing contractor.  Any materials supplied by a contractor e.g. ballast and \nnailers, must meet GAF's requirements as set forth in their current specifications.  \nPhysical properties of the membrane (tensile strength, elongation, cold flex, dimensional \nstability and lap joint strength) are on file at HUD Headquarters and GAF Materials \nCorporation. \n \nWIND AND FIRE CLASSIFICATION: \n \n Mechanically fastened roofing systems shall be designed to resist wind uplift forces as \ndetermined in the Wind Design Guide for Mechanically Fastened Single-Ply Roofing \nSystems, published by the Single Ply Roofing Institute (SPRI). \n \n Ballasted roofing systems shall be desi gned in accordance with the Wind Design Guide \nfor Ballasted Singly-Ply Roofing Systems, published by SPRI. \n \n Fire Classification shall be in accordance with  Underwriters Laboratories, Inc. (UL) or \nFactory Mutual Engineering Corporation (FM) construction details.  To qualify for fire \nrating and uplift resistance, the system shall be in the current UL or FM Listings. \n \nINSTALLATION: \n \n 1. General \n \n The RUBEROID roofing system shall only be installed by roofing contractors \napproved by GAF Materials Corporation.  The System shall be installed in \naccordance with GAF Materials Corporation's specifications and details in effect \nat the time of installation, and HUD Minimum Property Standards. \n \n 2. Substrate Preparation \n \n  Preparation of the substrate shall comply with the latest edition of the GAF \nMaterials Corporation RUBEROID Modified Bitumen Roofing Application and \nSpecifications Manual.  Design of the roof deck is the responsibility of the owner \nor his architect/engineer. \n \n 3. Insulation", "Specifications Manual.  Design of the roof deck is the responsibility of the owner \nor his architect/engineer. \n \n 3. Insulation \n \n  Use only the insulation type indicated in the RUBEROID specifications, or as \napproved in writing by GAF Mateials Corporation.  All insulation board shall be \nattached using the method as tested for wind uplift. \n-3- \n \n 4. Membrane \n \n  All RUBEROID roofing systems, incl uding insulation, shall be installed by a \nGAF Materials Corporation approved contractor.  Membrane installation, \nincluding placing, bonding, lap splicing, perimeter attachment, flashing, \nconstruction closure, walkway and other required work to provide a watertight \nroofing system, shall comply with GAF Materials Corporation specifications. \n \nINSPECTION: \n \n A designated representative of  GAF Materials Corporation shall make inspections of the \ninstallation at the following intervals: (1) prior to delivery of materials, to accept or reject \nthe surface of the roof deck to which the roofing system is to be applied; (2) during the \ninstallation--to inspect and approve the installation techniques and methods; and (3) upon \ncompletion--to give final approval to the installation. \n \nWARRANTY: \n \n A ten year GAF Materials Corporation Li berty Guarantee shall be provided for all \ninstallations.  The warranty shall automatically transfer to successors upon written notice \nto GAF Materials Corporation of such a transfer. \n \n GAF Materials Corporation hereby warrants to the owner of its roofing system, installed \nby an applicator approved by GAF Materials Corporation, that the system will remain in \na watertight condition and will retain at least 80% of its specified aged thermal resistance \nvalue, if applicable, for a period of ten years from the date of installation.  In the event of \nfailure of the aforesaid system to function as warranted above, whether on account of \ndefective materials, faulty installation or on account of normal processes of wear and \naging, GAF Materials Corporation will make, or cause to be made, repairs necessary to \nenable the system to perform as warranted above. \n \n GAF Materials Corporation's obligations to repair the system under this warranty shall \nnot be in force or effect unless: (1) GAF Materials Corporation is notified of any failure \nof the system covered by the warranty within thirty (30) days following such failure; (2) \nthe system is installed by an applicator approved by GAF Materials Corporation and (3) \nno alterations or repairs to the system are made without the prior written approval of \nGAF Materials Corporation as to the extent, methods and materials used. \n-4- \n \n GAF Materials Corporation assumes no liability for any failure of the system resulting \nfrom wind forces which exceed the design wind, nor for acts of God, including without \nlimitations, lightning or earthquake; nor for any failure of the system resulting from fire \nof any origin or cause, nor for any failure of the product caused by movement of the \nsubstrate or by structural defects of the building on which the system is applied; nor from \ndeliberate misuse of the product; nor for any failure of the system caused by leakage or \nany other cause from an adjacent structure. \n \nMANUFACTURER'S RESPONSIBILITIES: \n \n Issuance of this Materials Release (MR) commits the manufacturer to fulfill, as a \nminimum, the following: \n \n1. Produce, label and certify the material, product or system in strict accordance with the \nterms of this MR. \n \n2. Provide necessary corrective action in a timely manner for all cases of justified \ncomplaint, poor performance or failure reported by HUD. \n \n3. When requested, provide the FHA Standards, Office of Manufactured Housing \nPrograms, HUD Headquarters, with a representative list of properties in which the \nmaterial, product, or system has been used, including complete addresses or \ndescriptions of locations and dates of installation.", "material, product, or system has been used, including complete addresses or \ndescriptions of locations and dates of installation. \n \n4. Inform HUD, in advance, of changes in production facilities, methods, design of the \nproduct, company name, ownership or mailing address. \n \nEVALUATION: \n \n This MR shall be valid for a period of three ye ars from the date of initial issuance or most \nrecent renewal or revision, whichever is later.  The holder of this MR shall apply for \nrenewal or revision 90 days prior to the Review Date printed on this MR.  Submittals for \nrenewal or revision shall be sent to: \n \n  U. S. Department of Housing and Urban Development \n  Office of Manufactured Hous ing Programs, FHA Standards \n  451 7 th Street, SW, Room 9152 \n  Washington, DC  20410-8000 \n \n Appropriate User F ee shall be sent to: \n-5- \n \n  U. S. Department of Housing and Urban Development \n  Technical Suitabili ty of Products Fees \n  P. O. Box 954199 \n  St. Louis, MO  63195-4199 \n \n The holder of this MR may apply for revision at any time prior to the Review Date.  \nMinor revisions may be in the form of a supplement to the MR. \n \n If the Department determines that a pr oposed renewal or supplement constitutes a \nrevision, the appropriate User Fee for a revision will need to be submitted in accordance \nwith Code of Federal Regulations 24 CFR 200.934, \"User Fee System for the Technical \nSuitability of Products Program,\" and current User Fee Schedule. \n \nCANCELLATION: \n \n Failure to apply for a renewal or revision shall constitute a basis for cancellation of this \nMR.  HUD will notify the manufacturer that the MR may be canceled when: \n \n1. conditions under which the document was issued have changed so as to affect \nproduction of, or to compromise the integrity of the accepted material, product, or \nsystem, \n2. the manufacturer has changed its organizational form without notifying HUD, or \n \n3. the manufacturer has not complied with responsibilities  it assumed as a condition of \nHUD's acceptance. \n \n However, before cancellation, HUD will give  the manufacturer reasonable notice, in \nwriting, of the specific reasons for cancellation, and the opportunity to present views on \nwhy the MR should not be canceled.  No refund of fees will be made on a canceled \ndocument. \n \n ************************************************************************ \n This Materials Release is issued solely for the captioned firm, and is not transferable to \nany person or successor entity. \n ************************************************************************"], "vectors": [[-0.035037826746702194, 0.04473929852247238, 0.036645084619522095, -0.09679166972637177, 0.029057232663035393, -0.13249540328979492, -0.03486126661300659, 0.008913222700357437, -0.13338419795036316, -0.016827668994665146, -0.0523344986140728, 0.006204530596733093, 0.019393255934119225, -0.06292697787284851, -0.09297416359186172, -0.014438817277550697, -0.030841872096061707, -0.021531522274017334, -0.004944486077874899, 0.04262325540184975, 0.019804619252681732, 0.027254078537225723, -0.03656988590955734, -0.0034986273385584354, 0.03157765790820122, 0.017130745574831963, -0.04512298107147217, 0.061589792370796204, -0.036126043647527695, -0.006634126883000135, 0.02742706425487995, 0.10180098563432693, -0.04362761974334717, 0.025446631014347076, 0.06043995916843414, -0.026825077831745148, 0.014348017983138561, 0.005770848598331213, -0.08528990298509598, 0.07737557590007782, -0.026872120797634125, -0.06613371521234512, 0.01532907597720623, -0.01824560947716236, 0.05773043632507324, 0.004786949139088392, 0.006672711111605167, 0.00432570232078433, -0.0009018801501952112, -0.010438046418130398, 0.03159870207309723, 0.038414232432842255, 0.007867741398513317, -0.021011091768741608, 0.004346165806055069, 0.03704534471035004, -0.06728141754865646, 0.006812488